From a333b2cb1f494dd02f33c97f5061680be5936fbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 23:21:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add semantic check for `deco 0` architecture building
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

test_scotch_arch_build builds decomposition-described architectures
from weighted path graphs whose edge loads force the recursive
bipartition (loads within a factor of two keep parts contiguous; the
median edge of every interval carries the strictly largest load, hence
the strictly cheapest cut).  It then checks, by parsing the saved
"deco 1" data, that:

- the root domain holds all the terminals;
- the singleton leaves hold each path vertex exactly once;
- sibling singleton leaves hold path-ADJACENT vertices (the two ends
  of the last edge cut) — this is the property that detects terminal
  vertices paired with the wrong domain of the bipartition;
- the architecture is invariant with respect to the graph base value
  (tested with bases 0, 1 and 100000).

The existing test_scotch_arch_deco only exercises build/save/load
round-trips, so it cannot detect a structurally consistent but
mispaired decomposition tree.
